# Testing — Atlas World Service

## Suites & Commands

```bash
# Fast mid-iteration check (<15s)
./scripts/fastcheck.sh

# Full Gate 1 pre-ship suite
./scripts/precheck.sh --no-install

# Rust game server (server-rs/)
cd server-rs && cargo test

# Shared TypeScript contracts (contracts/)
cd contracts && pnpm test

# Script & content gates (Node 24 — pass explicit glob)
node scripts/check_content.mjs
node --test scripts/tests/*.test.mjs

# Atelier tool suites
node --test atelier/art-forge/tests/*.test.mjs
node --test atelier/mapforge/tests/*.test.mjs
node --test atelier/atlas-world-panels/tests/*.test.mjs

# React web client
cd client/react-client && CI=true npx react-scripts test --watchAll=false
```

## Conventions
- Inject simulated time (`SimClock` in `server-rs/src/core/clock.rs`) instead of sleeping in tests.
- Cover boundary edge cases (zeroes, negative ratios, overflow, unit-contract metre boundaries).
- Keep cargo light on laptops: Gate 1 caps workers via `ATLAS_MAX_WORKERS` (default `2`).

